            <ArticleTitle>Abdominal pain in children: a case of acalculous cholecystitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acalculous cholecystitis is a rare disease in children. Most cases are associated with systemic infections or with autoimmune pathologies, but it may also occur without predisposing factors. A case observed in an otherwise healthy child is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
